cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TRACE-ER Explorer or its dataset in your research or work,
  please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
title: TRACE-ER Explorer
abstract: >-
  TRACE-ER Explorer is a multi-state environmental risk screening prototype
  that integrates eight public U.S. federal and state data sources into a
  single facility-level index covering 527,983 regulated entities across
  Texas, Pennsylvania, New Mexico, and Maine. It produces a composite risk
  score for each facility based on EPA compliance history, toxic chemical
  releases, county-level pipeline incident history, and state-specific
  resource extraction activity, and delivers results through a Power BI
  dashboard and open data files.
